# {{project.name}}: the backend

The API, {{#if (eq language "java")}}in Java with Spring Boot{{/if}}{{#if (eq language "node")}}in Node with Express and Prisma{{/if}}{{#if (eq language "python")}}in Python with FastAPI and SQLAlchemy{{/if}}, on the EGRADX SDK {{sdkVersion}}. The project's
[README](../README.md) shows what is where. Run everything below from this folder.

## Access to the SDK's packages

Create a GitHub token (classic) with the scope `read:packages` and keep it in `GITHUB_TOKEN`:

```sh
export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...            # Windows PowerShell: $env:GITHUB_TOKEN = "ghp_..."
```

{{#if (eq language "java")}}
Then give Maven a server with the **same id** as the repository in `pom.xml`, in `~/.m2/settings.xml`:

```xml
<settings>
  <servers>
    <server>
      <id>egradx-sdk-github</id>
      <username>YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME</username>
      <password>${env.GITHUB_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
  </servers>
</settings>
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq language "node")}}
`.npmrc` already reads it, so `npm install` works as it is.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq language "python")}}
The Python packages are wheels on the GitHub release `python-v{{sdkVersion}}`. Download them into `egradx-wheels/`
(`pyproject.toml` installs from there):

```sh
python scripts/get_wheels.py           # or: gh release download python-v{{sdkVersion}} -R babulvaibhav/egradx-v1-workspace -p "*.whl" -D egradx-wheels
```
{{/if}}

## Run it

{{#if extra.compose}}
Start the services first, from the project's folder: `docker compose up -d`.
{{else}}
You need a PostgreSQL database named `{{project.module}}` (user `postgres`, password `postgres` by default).
{{/if}}
`.env.example` lists every setting; only `EGRADX_KEY_PASSPHRASE` has no default.

{{#if (eq language "java")}}
```sh
EGRADX_KEY_PASSPHRASE=change-me ./mvnw spring-boot:run
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq language "node")}}
```sh
npm install
npx prisma generate
EGRADX_KEY_PASSPHRASE=change-me npm run dev
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq language "python")}}
```sh
uv sync
EGRADX_KEY_PASSPHRASE=change-me uv run python -m {{project.module}}
```
{{/if}}

## Try it

```sh
# Sign in
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/egradx/auth/login -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"username":"ada@example.com","password":"demo-password"}' | sed 's/.*"accessToken":"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/')

# Create a note
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/notes -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"title":"First note"}'

# Its audit record, and the notice in everyone's bell
curl -s "http://localhost:8080/egradx/audit/events?action={{project.area}}.note.created" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
curl -s http://localhost:8080/egradx/notifications -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
{{#if cap.events}}

# The count an event handler keeps, a moment after the commit
curl -s http://localhost:8080/api/notes/stats -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
{{/if}}
```
